WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.752
(grunts)

00:00:03.211 --> 00:00:04.879
TORI:
I think that we kind of
take for granted

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:06.840
the amount of knowledge
and experience that we have

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.842
when we're heading out
into the backcountry.

00:00:09.926 --> 00:00:13.054
For us, it might just kind of
be your regular adventure

00:00:13.054 --> 00:00:15.765
but for others,
it's a huge endeavor

00:00:15.765 --> 00:00:18.435
and, and scary
and there's a lot to learn.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:22.981
JIM:
I can't believe that we just
rolled in here just before dark

00:00:22.981 --> 00:00:25.483
and found a gorgeous campsite.

00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:29.195
-(Wesley giggling)
-TORI: Wes, you are in
a very good mood this morning.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:32.949
This one, on the other hand,
this one... is up to no good.

00:00:33.908 --> 00:00:37.328
(Huddy gurgling)

00:00:37.328 --> 00:00:37.954
Ow!

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:41.916
JIM:
Water's boiling, honey.

00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:45.253
TORI:
Do you just wanna
do oatmeal this morning?

00:00:45.253 --> 00:00:46.671
JIM:
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:46.671 --> 00:00:49.007
It's oatmeal or no-meal
in these parts.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.634
TORI:
For Wesley's meals
in the backcountry,

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.386
because of his low muscle tone,

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.055
he isn't able
to chew efficiently.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.390
So, we puree all of his food

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.810
or give him as much soft,
mashable food as possible.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.812
It can be a little bit
more challenging

00:01:02.812 --> 00:01:05.982
if we are trying to live off
the land as much as possible.

00:01:05.982 --> 00:01:08.026
Foraging for foods
and things like that for him,

00:01:08.026 --> 00:01:09.069
we do have to make sure
it's something

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:11.362
that he's gonna be able
to eat, first of all,

00:01:11.362 --> 00:01:13.782
and also it's gonna be
easy on his tummy.

00:01:13.782 --> 00:01:16.493
JIM:
I think Wesley is just
responding so well

00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:17.243
to being in nature.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.037
But I think he's
also just happy

00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:21.289
to spend more
quality time with us.

00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:22.832
He just seems to be,
you know,

00:01:22.832 --> 00:01:24.751
more engaged
with his surrounding.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.461
Don't you Wes, huh?

00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:29.964
You little champion,
my best bud. Yes you are!

00:01:29.964 --> 00:01:32.550
(Wesley and Huddy murmur)

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.219
So that was some
pretty good feedback

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:35.678
we got from
the physiotherapist

00:01:35.678 --> 00:01:37.597
about just getting
Wesley outdoors?

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:40.058
TORI:
Totally. And I think
it'll be a great thing

00:01:40.058 --> 00:01:42.143
to prepare him
for going to school.

00:01:42.143 --> 00:01:43.061
'Cause he's starting school

00:01:43.061 --> 00:01:44.312
pretty much
right when we get back.

00:01:44.312 --> 00:01:47.065
JIM:
I'm probably gonna cry
when we drop him off at school.

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:48.316
-TORI: Oh, yeah. For sure.
-JIM: 'Cause our special
little boy,

00:01:48.316 --> 00:01:51.611
he can't really communicate
and it's a big day for him.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:54.072
He's gonna make some friends,
he's gonna learn,

00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:55.949
you know, they have
devices for him there

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:57.909
that we can't really fit
in our house.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.371
But, I think it's gonna be great
for his development

00:02:01.371 --> 00:02:03.873
and for him
to make some friends.

00:02:03.873 --> 00:02:06.334
TORI:
He's never really been
away from us for that--

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:07.919
-JIM: No he hasn't. No.
-TORI: That long.
You know what I mean?

00:02:07.919 --> 00:02:09.129
JIM:
Your brother's gonna
go to school

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:10.713
-and then learn stuff.
-(Huddy babbles)

00:02:10.713 --> 00:02:13.299
TORI:
As far as when we
one day live off-grid,

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:16.469
unless we're prepared to do
some serious homeschooling

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:17.929
for him and Hudson--

00:02:17.929 --> 00:02:19.139
JIM:
Yeah so that's the other thing,

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.850
homeschooling is
a lot of work as well.

00:02:22.225 --> 00:02:24.102
We'll find a way
to make it work, you know?

00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:26.354
-TORI: Yeah.
-JIM: We'll find a way
to do both things.

00:02:26.354 --> 00:02:27.564
TORI:
When we first started dating

00:02:27.564 --> 00:02:31.025
there was this romanticized
fantasy of living off-grid

00:02:31.025 --> 00:02:33.069
in a log cabin
in the middle of nowhere,

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:35.155
which sounded beautiful.

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:38.741
But, having Wesley now
and his needs,

00:02:38.741 --> 00:02:41.619
I do worry about
living there full-time.

00:02:42.245 --> 00:02:44.080
I'm excited about it,
I'm nervous.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.708
I think that I'm just more
of the logistical person

00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:48.126
when it comes to the kids.

00:02:48.918 --> 00:02:50.712
I don't wanna be
irresponsible with it.

00:02:50.712 --> 00:02:52.172
I don't wanna be
taking Wesley,

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.840
who does have
these complex needs,

00:02:54.132 --> 00:02:56.676
so far away from help.

00:02:57.427 --> 00:02:58.928
To start, I'm really
looking forward

00:02:58.928 --> 00:03:01.055
to having that
off-grid property

00:03:01.055 --> 00:03:03.141
that we can go to
a couple times a year

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.686
and gradually make it home.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:10.106
JIM:
(whistles) North,
time to do dishes.

00:03:10.106 --> 00:03:10.982
(North barks)

